description:
FILED s514a (Opus, 2026-10-10), found while writing lib/Storable.pm (thaw's `$flags` argument vs `$Storable::flags`).

Reproducer (scratch/s514a/pr/shadowq.pl), perl 5.40.3 vs PCL main 4d2fc9f0:

    package Foo;
    $Foo::flags = 6;
    sub get { my ($flags) = @_; return defined $flags ? $flags : $Foo::flags }
    print get(), " ", get(3), "\n";          # perl "6 3"   PCL " 3"
    sub get2 { my $flags; return $Foo::flags }
    print get2(), "\n";                      # perl "6"     PCL ""

Same as a program and as a `use`d module.  The emission spells both the lexical and the package variable as the SAME symbol `Foo::$flags` (`(p-if (p-defined $flags) $flags Foo::$flags)` read in package Foo), so the `let` of the lexical captures the qualified read.  A qualified `$PKG::name` must never resolve to a lexical (perl: a package-qualified name is always the global).  Family: #470 (identity-promoted file lexical aliases the package variable), #328.

Workaround in lib/Storable.pm: the lexical is named `$flg`.  Silent (no drop, no die): a value is wrong.

CONFIRMED s514 (Fable, 2026-10-10 10:50, main cc3caca6 = code 4d2fc9f0, probe ~/pcl-agent-scratch/s513/review/p514a/shadowq.pl through probe.sh): perl `6 3` / `6`, PCL ` 3` / `` as filed; and the `our` spelling too -- `our $x = 'pkg'; sub get3 { my $x = 'lex'; return "$x $Foo::x" }` prints `lex pkg` in perl and `lex lex` in PCL.  A qualified `$PKG::name` read inside a sub must resolve to the package cell even when a same-named lexical is in scope: the lexical's `let` must bind a RENAMED symbol (the my-shadow mechanism of DECIDED Direction D), or the qualified read must spell the global cell explicitly.  Silent wrong in ordinary module code (Storable's own $flags idiom) -- the convergent class of docs/production-readiness-review-s513.md; a candidate for the next correctness batch.
